        "Allan H. MacDonald",
        "Pablo Jarillo-Herrero",
        "Rafi Bistritzer"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Magic-angle twisted bilayer graphene revealed tunable correlated and superconducting phases, making moiré materials a new laboratory for quantum matter.",
        "attribution": "Bistritzer and MacDonald predicted the flat-band mechanism, while Jarillo-Herrero's group observed correlated phases and superconductivity.",
        "maturity": "The results triggered extensive reproduction and follow-up, but the phase diagram and mechanisms remain active research subjects.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The relationship between superconductivity, correlated insulators, and disorder is unresolved, so the physical interpretation is still developing."
        ]
      }
    },
